<!--Post: 224--><!--Time: 1086670086-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST224"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, June 07, 2004 - 9:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Was the recording of BTK&#39;s call to the police following the Nancy Fox murder edited for public listening? I believe so.  <BR> <BR>Here&#39;s a transcript of the call: <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR>OPERATOR 1: Dispatcher. <BR> <BR>BTK: Yes. You will find a homicide at 843 South Pershing. Nancy Fox. <BR> <BR>OPERATOR 1: I&#39;m sorry sir I can&#39;t understand you. What is the address? <BR> <BR>OPERATOR 2: I believe 843 South Pershing. <BR> <BR>BTK: That is correct. <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>The second operator in the above transcript interrupts the conversation with no introduction, etc. Also, BTK doesn&#39;t even seem to notice that she&#39;s a different voice than the first operator. Those two factors tell me the second operator and BTK had previous dialogue that was edited from the recording. &#40;Unless the second operator was the person who placed the call for BTK, but how many telephone operators interrupt &#34;911&#34; calls???&#41; <BR> <BR>Also, there is an unusual pause after the first operator asks BTK to repeat the address. The second operator finally speaks, but why did BTK seem to wait for her, especially considering the circumstances? How did he even know she was there? I&#39;d think BTK would have immediately repeated the address. <BR> <BR> <BR>Regardless, the second operator sounds almost in shock when she repeats the address that the first operator couldn&#39;t understand. Why? I believe after BTK mentioned the name of the victim, he went on to describe in detail what happened to her and that he was responsible. At that point, the first operator asked for the address again and the somewhat shocked second operator repeated it for her.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 224-->
<!--Post: 227--><!--Time: 1086726374-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST227"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 08, 2004 - 1:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Perhaps you could also argue that the opening &#34;Yes&#34; from BTK may have been a reply to a previous question.He may have mentioned something about the murder right off and maybe that&#39;s why the initial operator stayed on the line!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 227-->
<!--Post: 231--><!--Time: 1086811762-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST231"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Warren_b<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Warren_b<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, June 09, 2004 - 1:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sean, perhaps the question was, &#34;Do you have an emergency?&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 231-->
<!--Post: 232--><!--Time: 1086813669-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST232"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, June 09, 2004 - 1:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To which I would have expected,&#34;This is 911 isn&#39;t it&#34;. Seriously, whatever it was it does seem slighlty out of place and the theory goes to the possibility that call was edited. <BR>As it happens, there a post elsehwere that reports a detective &#40;name escapes me right now&#41; stating he believed the called placed was made by the killer &#40;BTK&#41;, &#34;because he knew too many details about her&#34;.So it does appear that the call had been edited.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 232-->
<!--Post: 237--><!--Time: 1086832643-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST237"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Muskogee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Muskogee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, June 09, 2004 - 6:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sean, they didn&#39;t have 911 back then.  &#34;What is your emergency?&#34;, &#34;Do you have an emergency?&#34;, etc. are common ways dispatchers answer the phone.  I&#39;m not discounting your theory that BTK could have answered, &#34;Yes...&#34; to another question and that some of the tape at the beginning is being withheld, I&#39;m simply saying it could also be something as mundane as Warren suggests.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 237-->
<!--Post: 240--><!--Time: 1086875891-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST240"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, June 10, 2004 - 6:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I did it again, that part was just a joke Musk, and apologies to Warren, I wasn&#39;t in any way disregarding his suggestion.It is probably the most obvious one.The point was simply that the message does appear edited.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 240-->
<!--Post: 249--><!--Time: 1086908991-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST249"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Muskogee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Muskogee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, June 10, 2004 - 4:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dang message boards...it&#39;s always hard to convey whether a message is serious or not &#40;at least, it&#39;s hard for me!&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 249-->
<!--Post: 255--><!--Time: 1086965158-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST255"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jenkins<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jenkins<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 11, 2004 - 7:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I always did find that pause between BTK and Op 2 somewhat odd. Must have been edited for public. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 255-->
<!--Post: 510--><!--Time: 1090145058-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST510"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scream187<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scream187<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, July 18, 2004 - 3:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe BTK was playing a recording and thats why he couldn&#39;t repeat the address right away, might have been caught off guard... needed to rewind or to say it &#34;live&#34;. I think the second operator sortof saved his ass. He only he had to say is &#34;That is correct&#34; instead of the whole address. That would also fit the theory that the way he says &#34;that is correct&#34; is diffrent from the rest and that its probably what his real voice sounds like. He wasnt planning on saying it since he didnt think the dispatcher might not hear the address correctly the first time around. <BR> <BR>Then again maybe the tape was just edited. But i think my &#34;theory&#34; would explain the gap in a reasonable way.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 510-->
<!--Post: 1216--><!--Time: 1097779332-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1216"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nostone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nostone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, October 14, 2004 - 11:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I actually don&#39;t think that the &#34;That is correct&#34; sounds all THAT different from the rest.  Just not as slow and deliberate.  I&#39;m quite sure it&#39;s been edited, though.  That second dispatcher does sound mighty spooked, so BTK probably did give more details than we are allowed to hear. <BR> <BR>I really don&#39;t think it was a recording.  Tape recording/playing devices were bulky and cumbersome back then, especially if you wanted to be incognito.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1216-->
<!--Post: 1462--><!--Time: 1101823484-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1462"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, November 30, 2004 - 6:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I read the article by Charlie Otero where he stated that the police never allowed him to hear the Fox call recording. I find that incomprehensible and ethically reprehensible. Not in my wildest imagination could I fathom the police making such a glaring and bumbling step as that. They will have a difficult time denying coverup, unless thay claim incompetence: And I have a criminal justice and police trained background! How many more people have died because of this. Perhaps they are hoping that BTK will become senile and disabled and therefore unable to continue his serial killer career. <BR> <BR>As a psychologist, I have to have an ethics course yearly to maintain my certification. Surely, the law enforcement community should do the same. Ethics aren&#39;t necessarily about personal integrity, but how to act in sticky situations to avoid appearing compromised. Due diligence, WPD!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1462-->
<!--Post: 1751--><!--Time: 1102796274-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1751"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bodycheck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bodycheck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 11, 2004 - 12:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Man....i hate to say it...but the lingo and pronunciation sound like a cop or some type of law enforcement person to me... <BR> <BR>&#34;Homicide,&#40;victims name&#41;&#34; .... &#34;that is correct&#34;... <BR> <BR>Sounds too much like a cop writing a report... <BR> <BR>what do i know...Im a newbie <BR> <BR>B<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1751-->
